       "Source(title='AI in Agriculture: Overview and Benefits | Microsoft AI', url='https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/copilot/ai-knowledge/ai-in-agriculture', content='AI in agriculture is optimizing the supply chain by making real-time crop monitoring, intelligent logistics, dynamic resource allocation, and proactive risk management possible.\\n AI-powered automation is revolutionizing the handling, forecasting, sorting, and packaging across harvesting and post-harvesting processes.\\n By forecasting demand, predicting spoilage, and redistributing surplus crops, AI tools can help reduce food waste. [...] AI is used in agriculture to optimize supply chain efficiency, automate harvesting, manage food distribution—helping farmers boost yields, cut waste, and quickly adapt to changing conditions.\\n The future of AI agriculture lies in autonomous, data-driven farming systems that adapt in real time to environmental and market shifts. These resilient systems have the ability to make decisions on planting, irrigation, harvesting, and distribution, in turn reducing food waste and boosting yields. [...] Generative AI in agriculture uses a combination of machine learning, computer vision, and predictive analytics to boost farming efficiency, resulting in more optimized supply chains and streamlined operations, and less food waste.\\n\\n## Key takeaways')"
